# Code owners: the people GitHub asks to review a pull request that touches a path.
# The last matching pattern wins, and listing two owners means either one can approve.
#
# There are two maintainers and each is the other's reviewer, so both own everything. A pull
# request's author is never asked to review their own change.
#
# Market discovery is split between them in two lanes (see
# docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-14-market-discovery.md). The lane says who writes the code, not
# who reviews it, so lanes are not repeated here as patterns: a single-owner pattern would leave
# the author as the only owner of their own files, and nobody could approve those pull requests.

